(7770768, 1290253, 88235, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Barroness:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations, 10 from me. I have gone up the mountain to Grandview so many times hoping for an image of this bridge like this one and I could never find the spot, it is such a beautiful bridge. This is an amazing image of this bridge. STUNNING WORK! </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>Thanks! I did a drone shoot for a house up on Tweed that overlooked the bridge directly from the west side. They are sooo lucky. I have lived in Nyack for the last 5 years and absolutely love the bridge. The shape of it, the changing colors, the fact that they included a bike / pedestrian area... It is all just great. 
<br/>
<br/>I ride bike as well and have noticed a couple of good spots on the east side of the bridge. The EF International Language campus may have a couple of nice views. I always can glimpse the bridge as I ride down the hill from there. 
<br/>
<br/>Here is my favorite picture of the bridge. It was done by someone I follow on facebook who does some amazing night time photography (my favorite) <a href="https://www.facebook.com/share/p/sRGFTCB6JXL3418r/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">https://www.facebook.com/share/p/sRGFTCB6JXL3418r/</a>
<br/>I''ve never shared a facebook pic trough a URL before, so I hope it comes through.</td>', 'Originally posted by Barroness: Congratulations, 10 from me. I have gone up the mountain to Grandview so many times hoping for an image of this bridge like this one and I could never find the spot, it is such a beautiful bridge. This is an amazing image of this bridge. STUNNING WORK! 

Thanks! I did a drone shoot for a house up on Tweed that overlooked the bridge directly from the west side. They are sooo lucky. I have lived in Nyack for the last 5 years and absolutely love the bridge. The shape of it, the changing colors, the fact that they included a bike / pedestrian area... It is all just great. 

I ride bike as well and have noticed a couple of good spots on the east side of the bridge. The EF International Language campus may have a couple of nice views. I always can glimpse the bridge as I ride down the hill from there. 

Here is my favorite picture of the bridge. It was done by someone I follow on facebook who does some amazing night time photography (my favorite) https://www.facebook.com/share/p/sRGFTCB6JXL3418r/
I''ve never shared a facebook pic trough a URL before, so I hope it comes through.', '2024-10-05 18:13:25.000000', NULL, 0),
